### 6.3 The realization

A realization gives each site a machine type; a site it does not name takes the default.

Given: default `f64`, 1 sites typed apart, 2 parameters stored otherwise.

**Every value the program stores**, the solver's decisions, with its type and where the type comes from:

| Site | Operation | Type | From |
|--------------------------|----------------------------|----------|-----------|
| `Block.apply/%5` | `gelu %4` | `f64` | the default |
| `Block.apply/%8` | `add x, %7` | `f64` | the default |
| `Linear.apply/%3` | `dot x, w` | `f32` | the record |
| `Linear.apply/%5` | `add %3, b` | `f64` | the default |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%3` | `pow 2 x` | `f64` | the default |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%4` | `mean axis model %3` | `f64` | the default |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%5` | `real eps` | `f64` | the default |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%7` | `sqrt %6` | `f64` | the default |
| `RMSNorm.apply/%10` | `mul %8, γ` | `f64` | the default |
| `loss/%6` | `pow 2 %5` | `f64` | the default |
| `loss/%7` | `mean %6` | `f64` | the default |

